description:
SKILLS REQUIREMENTS:
Proficiency in English, MS Office and Google Suite;
Hands-on experience with spreadsheets and propriety software such as Quick books;
Basic knowledge in INTUIT PRO SERIES PLATFORM
Basic knowledge in US TAX Preparation;
Proven bookkeeping experience;
Solid understanding of basic bookkeeping and accounting payable or receivable principles;
Proven ability to calculate, post and manage accounting figures and financial records;
Data entry skills along with a knack for numbers
Customer Service orientation and negotiation skills;
High degree of accuracy and attention to details.
Job Type: Full-time
Work Location: Remote

Conducting calls and going on media rounds to increase pick-ups and/or ensure attendance in
press conferences and other events, or simply to catch up;
Accompanying media during media familiarization tours, offsite press events, and the like.
Handling media invitations, logistics preparation, and onsite coordination;
Providing support and media management and handling during face-to-face/online/hybrid
events and conferences;
Documenting media elements during events through photos, videos, or media summaries.
Monitoring coverage, helping prepare media reports and following through on additional
opportunities/responding to additional inquiries from the media.
Monitoring publications, online and social media and ensuring that all industry updates and
movements are noted, documented and shared with the relevant teams;
Helping maintain and update, as necessary, a master media database, constantly growing and
improving to include the correct information:
o Name of editor/reporter/influencer;
o Affiliation: Name of newspaper, magazine, TV station, website, vlog, etc.;
o Office address and telephone/mobile phone and social media;
o Birthday and any other relevant occasions;
o Any additional information: hobbies, likes, and dislikes.
o History of Perceptions’ liaison with the media/influencer
Keeping the media birthday and Christmas gift lists updated, ordering/preparing the gifts and
complimentary cards, and providing the PR and Management teams with regular and on-time
media birthday notices.
Providing research for media trainings, including media lists, industry trends and reports.
Coordinating with external partners, suppliers, and vendors when needed;
Maintaining and informing other departments of up-to-date schedules of meetings and
appointments of the Media Services team;
Taking notes and putting together contact reports of official meetings with the media and
amongst the internal Media Services team.
Pay: Php25,000.00 - Php30,000.00 per month
Benefits:
Flexible schedule
Work Location: Remote

About Us:
Verified First is a booming tech company on a mission to deliver cutting-edge technology transforming how organizations protect their people. As a constant recipient of the "Best Places to Work" award, you can be sure we'll invest in you as both a professional and a person. We're looking for people like you - ambitious, hard-working, and fun - to join our team!
Summary:
The Client Services Representative will assist our clients with questions, concerns, and educate them on Verified First’s products and services. The successful person in this role will encourage a direct and positive relationship between Verified First and our clients.
How our Client Services Representative spends their time:
Provide world-class service for client inquiries via email, phone, or chat in a professional and empathetic manner;
Meet the goals of the Client Service team around response times and resolution times for client cases;
Educate clients on searches, forms needed for searches, and the adverse action process;
Assist clients with creating new user accounts, processing orders, and training clients on how to use the background screening application;
Train new clients on the billing process;
Assist other departments in obtaining information and forms needed from clients to perform searches;
Perform other duties as assigned.
What you bring:
A positive, solution-focused attitude;
An interest in learning more about application support and service delivery;
An interest in continuous improvement;
Ability to maintain regular and punctual attendance;
You work well independently but understand the importance of teamwork;
Strong verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to effectively facilitate and adjust communication styles to the audience.
Preferred Qualifications:
High School Diploma or equivalent required;
1 - 2 years of experience in a Client Services Department in a call center environment;
Working knowledge of G-Suite and Microsoft Office products;
Experience in Salesforce is preferred;
Background screening experience is preferred;
Proven ability to build, nurture, and retain client relationships;
Able to sit at a desk and work on a computer for prolonged periods of time;
Navigate between multiple windows/browsers with ease, perform extensive internet research, and type 45 WPM.
What we bring:
Work-life balance: Enjoy your free time with no weekends, paid holidays, and paid time off starting on your first day;
Growth: Continue to learn with continuous education, career pathing, and ongoing training. You won’t stall here, growth is part of our success;
Outstanding Culture: In our remote work environment, we prioritize team-building through engaging meetings and events, including town halls, Office Olympics, and culture conversations. These activities are vital for strengthening our connections and embodying our company values.
What are the next steps?
Our Talent Acquisition Specialist will be reviewing resumes. If you are among one of the qualified candidates you will receive an emaill to schedule an interview.
Verified First is proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We expect all team members to have an understanding of, and commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion.
The pay for this remote position varies based on experience, job responsibilities, and geographical location to comply with state-specific pay regulations.
JIqysfnIhk

About the Team
We are Quadcode, a fintech company excelling in financial brokerage activities and delivering advanced financial products to our global clientele. Our flagship product, an internal trading platform, is offered as a Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) solution to other brokers.
IQ Option is a globally recognized financial broker, renowned for its cutting-edge online trading platform. Founded in 2013, IQ Option has become one of the world’s leading online trading platforms, operating in more than 13 languages and offering access to Forex, CFDs, and Options.
We are currently looking for a motivated and results-driven VIP Account Manager to join our Sales Team and provide premium services to our high-value clients.
Tasks:
Conduct proactive outreach to potential and existing VIP clients through calls, written communication, and internal CRM tools;
Promote company products and services to high-value clients;
Apply effective negotiation techniques to convert leads into long-term customers;
Develop and implement initiatives to increase client satisfaction and retention;
Build and maintain strong, long-term relationships as a trusted advisor;
Monitor client activity and identify opportunities for growth and engagement;
Maintain accurate records of client interactions in the CRM system.
Requirements:
English proficiency at B2 level or higher;
Native or bilingual proficiency in Thai;
Bachelor’s degree in Economics, Finance, Business, or a related field;
Proven experience in the financial industry, preferably in sales, account management, or business development;
Strong communication, negotiation, and relationship-building skills;
Result-oriented mindset and ability to work in a fast-paced environment;
High level of responsibility and professionalism when working with VIP clients.
What We Offer:
Remote work model;
Competitive remuneration;
Professional courses: from Coursera to Harvard;
Friendly, enjoyable and positive environment.
With a team of 500+ creative and tech-driven people across the globe, Quadcode is the place where ideas turn into impact, where every project is a chance to grow, innovate, and make your mark. Join us today, and let's shape the future of fintech together! Note: All applications will be treated with strict confidence. We thank all applicants for their interest, however, only those candidates selected for interviews will be contacted. #LI-NK1
With a team of 500+ creative and tech-driven people across the globe, Quadcode is the place where ideas turn into impact, where every project is a chance to grow, innovate, and make your mark.
Join us today, and let's shape the future of fintech together!
